  <static seed="507" source="Library/Michigan/Chap16Sec5/Q45.pg">
    <statement><p>The density, <m>\delta</m>, of the cylinder
<m>x^2+y^2\le 1</m>, <m>0\le z\le 5</m>
varies with the distance, <m>r</m>, from the <m>z</m>-axis:
<me>\delta = 1 + r\mbox{ g}/\mbox{cm}^3.</me>
Find the mass of the cylinder, assuming  <m>x,y,z</m> are in cm.</p>
<p>mass = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><em>(Include .)</em></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>26.1799\ {\rm g}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>r</m> first, we have
<me>\mbox{mass} = \int_0^{2\pi}\int_0^{5}\int_0^{1}(1+r)r\,dr\,dz\,d\theta =
  \int_0^{2\pi}\int_0^{5} \left(1\frac{r^2}2+\frac{r^3}3 \right)
  \Bigg|_0^{1}\,dz\,d\theta</me>
<me>= 2\pi \cdot 5\cdot
  \left(\frac{1}2+\frac{1}3\right) = \frac{25}{3}\pi\mbox{ g}.</me>



</solution>
